      "value": "1-overview1. Overview\n---------------------\n\nProduct data in the Zimmermann SFCC platform is managed through a **master catalogue** (`zimmermann-catalog`) with per-site **storefront catalogues** for navigation and category assignment. Product content (rich text, editorial imagery) is managed in **Contentful CMS**.\n\nAP21 is the system of record for all product data. Product data flows from AP21 into SFCC via **MuleSoft** — there is no direct AP21 → SFCC integration. MuleSoft acts as the integration layer, transforming and routing product data into SFCC catalogue XML imports.\n\n---\n\n2-product-data-architecture2. Product Data Architecture\n-------------------------------------------------------\n\nDefaultnoneAP21 (ERP — system of record for products)\n│\n└──► MuleSoft (integration layer — transform + route)\n│\n└──► zimmermann-catalog (SFCC master catalogue)\n│ products + variants + attributes\n│\n├──► zimmermann-au-storefront-catalog (AU nav categories)\n├──► zimmermann-uk-storefront-catalog (UK nav categories)\n├──► zimmermann-us-storefront-catalog (US domestic nav categories)\n├──► zimmermann-us-intl-storefront-catalog (US International / Global-e nav categories)\n├──► zimmermann-eu-storefront-catalog (EU nav categories)\n├──► zimmermann-eu-intl-storefront-catalog (EU International / Global-e nav categories)\n├──► zimmermann-hk-storefront-catalog (HK nav categories)\n└──► zimmermann-me-storefront-catalog (ME nav categories)\nContentful CMS\n│\n└──► PWA Kit (editorial content: banners, editorial copy, lookbook)\nvia Contentful Delivery API\n\n---\n\n3-master-catalogue-structure3. Master Catalogue Structure\n---------------------------------------------------------\n\n**Catalogue ID:**`zimmermann-catalog`\n\n### 31-category-hierarchy-all-storefront-catalogues3.1 Category Hierarchy (all storefront catalogues)\n\n| Position | Category ID | Display Name | Sub-categories |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | `new-arrivals` | New | — |\n| 2 | `clothin